## Non-functional requirements

- Keep local development inexpensive and reproducible.
- Do not require real secrets or paid services for tests.
- Apply the `[[ ui_style ]]` design preset with `[[ ui_layout ]]` composition while preserving semantic HTML and a logical reading order.
- Target WCAG 2.2 AA where applicable, including keyboard operation, visible focus, contrast-safe content, accessible forms, and reduced-motion alternatives.
- Keep visual effects CSS-first, responsive, and usable on mid-range mobile devices.

## MVP features

- A runnable [[ project_type ]] starter.
- Health or command smoke coverage appropriate to the profile.
- A responsive frontend using centralized semantic tokens and reusable accessible components.

## Out of scope

- Production deployment and cloud resource provisioning.
- Optional features not enabled in `project.yaml`.

## Acceptance criteria

- A new contributor can install dependencies, run the application, and execute tests from the README.
- No live cloud, database, or LLM service is required by the default test suite.
- Light, dark, and system theme modes remain readable; selected effects degrade gracefully when unsupported or reduced motion is requested.

